                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f104ab45-8c5c-3b5b-908c-f307fe3aa333",
                        "entry_id": "cb4ca7b4-680d-3ddd-a6d3-7e2854c74db0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "cecha tego, co kobiece"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "18c0bc87-9159-4e3b-b739-87be3889535d",
                                "sense_id": "f104ab45-8c5c-3b5b-908c-f307fe3aa333",
                                "text": "Niesłychany sukces Nowej Heloizy, apologia miłości, kobiecości, uczuć, nie mogą jednak przesłonić przesłania innego z dzieł wielkiego genewczyka - Emila, traktatu w pięciu księgach, poświęconego wychowaniu dzieci"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e81f9a4c-2d8e-4c6f-9fff-be58feae9268",
                        "source_entry_id": "cb4ca7b4-680d-3ddd-a6d3-7e2854c74db0",
                        "source_sense_id": "f104ab45-8c5c-3b5b-908c-f307fe3aa333",
                        "target_lang_word": "womanliness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "womanliness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d38f4994-1c06-310b-a9fb-17096eeb18b9",
                                        "entry_id": "58be5a86-2225-303e-ab23-3662f3f57b9b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being a woman; femininity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3b69b97-7160-43f1-8c27-9b67509ff6d3",
                                                "sense_id": "d38f4994-1c06-310b-a9fb-17096eeb18b9",
                                                "text": "As she walked along to-day, for all her bouncing handsome womanliness, you could sometimes see her twelfth year in her cheeks, or her ninth sparkling from her eyes; and even her fifth would flit over the curves of her mouth now and then."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5fe65128-d87a-4af6-b243-adfd2db1a423",
                        "source_entry_id": "cb4ca7b4-680d-3ddd-a6d3-7e2854c74db0",
                        "source_sense_id": "f104ab45-8c5c-3b5b-908c-f307fe3aa333",
                        "target_lang_word": "womanhood",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "womanhood",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c74c1085-3714-33b1-b165-ac3079463b7b",
                                        "entry_id": "343e5a48-161b-3f88-8f32-98eb70d549c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state or condition of being a woman, as contrasted with being a girl, man, boy, or nonbinary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8eebcb09-0e00-467e-95a4-8fde50f88a19",
                                                "sense_id": "c74c1085-3714-33b1-b165-ac3079463b7b",
                                                "text": "She was a vigorous youth poised on the brink of womanhood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "360a3cd6-447a-47b8-b7d3-1a8817a6a977",
                                                "sense_id": "c74c1085-3714-33b1-b165-ac3079463b7b",
                                                "text": "\"I swear, even in this most holy hour of completed Womanhood, that I will abandon Evil and cherish Good.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5935bf42-b88e-3cca-b536-0139bb4b7274",
                                        "entry_id": "343e5a48-161b-3f88-8f32-98eb70d549c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "All of the women of a given place, area, or subgroup regarded collectively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ae4434b-3fde-424e-9c44-0f8becd173f3",
                                                "sense_id": "5935bf42-b88e-3cca-b536-0139bb4b7274",
                                                "text": "There was only one thing to be done: call out, start the alarm, set the heather on fire! Awaken the womanhood of America to free the motherhood of the world!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81fb5d73-f52b-48f1-95a6-ca2b6482fff5",
                                                "sense_id": "5935bf42-b88e-3cca-b536-0139bb4b7274",
                                                "text": "[…]the white women, several of whom had been watching the massacre of the Negro men, pounced on the Negress. I do not wish to be understood as saying that these women were representatives of the womanhood of East St. Louis. Their faces showed, all too plainly, exactly who and what they were."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89097a6e-e5f7-476a-8097-e07f292581df",
                                                "sense_id": "5935bf42-b88e-3cca-b536-0139bb4b7274",
                                                "text": "What hast thou done, / O womanhood of France, / Mother and daughter, sister, sweetheart, wife, / What hast thou done, amid this fateful strife. // To prove the pride of thine inheritance / In this fair land of freedom and romance?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc00a27f-58ff-34ba-849b-e1a6960a29d5",
                                        "entry_id": "343e5a48-161b-3f88-8f32-98eb70d549c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The idealized nature of a woman: all of the characteristics traditionally and ideally ascribed to womanliness regarded collectively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae455a8e-6ea1-4ec9-8276-402d1dbd77da",
                                                "sense_id": "fc00a27f-58ff-34ba-849b-e1a6960a29d5",
                                                "text": "She had cast off the terror of the leaping flame, the cold power of judgment that was even now being done, and the wise sadness of the tombs - cast them off and put them behind her, like the white shroud she wore, and now stood out the incarnation of lovely tempting womanhood, made more perfect - and in a way more spiritual - than ever woman was before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51a619df-a470-48ac-ba8d-996bcbe2e840",
                                                "sense_id": "fc00a27f-58ff-34ba-849b-e1a6960a29d5",
                                                "text": "From the kitchen comes the even murmur of their voices. Mother and daughter: the protocols of womanhood being passed on, generation to generation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5ebbd98-9c92-30a3-8f5d-0d77712e28d3",
                                        "entry_id": "343e5a48-161b-3f88-8f32-98eb70d549c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The self-concept of a woman with respect to her possession of the various qualities traditionally and ideally ascribed to womanliness; a woman's sense or view of herself as being more or less womanly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9572817d-7f24-31fe-98ca-def1e5b2ce2c",
                                        "entry_id": "343e5a48-161b-3f88-8f32-98eb70d549c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The female genitalia, especially the vulva."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "euphemistic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e396b98-d3f2-4c88-9255-8911e2bd8a7c",
                                                "sense_id": "9572817d-7f24-31fe-98ca-def1e5b2ce2c",
                                                "text": "Easing down to her panties slowly as if investigating a carrier of a dangerous plague, both hands were quivering like it was contagious while feeling extraordinarily alarmed, he commenced to inspect her womanhood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6f0c69b2-c826-41a6-9ffb-1fc1a3491c20",
                        "source_entry_id": "cb4ca7b4-680d-3ddd-a6d3-7e2854c74db0",
                        "source_sense_id": "f104ab45-8c5c-3b5b-908c-f307fe3aa333",
                        "target_lang_word": "femininity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "femininity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03b3028c-8d04-3fd2-95b2-5214bc17481c",
                                        "entry_id": "763ed8aa-1631-343c-bd63-6d940c17c9e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The sum of all attributes that are feminine or convey womanhood."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86a31629-6dd1-4449-8945-72fbab775ad7",
                                                "sense_id": "03b3028c-8d04-3fd2-95b2-5214bc17481c",
                                                "text": "It's almost eerie, in the wake of the Lawrence Summers controversy, to encounter the words of an earlier Harvard president, John Kirkland, a \"friend and mentor\" of Elizabeth's, who advised her that if any woman \"is raised by genius and knowledge above the level of her sex, her neglect of attention appropriate to the best half of creation, attentions called femininities, will more than counterbalance all her advantages and reduce her below other women.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc7b8635-4cce-4aa4-b9f6-f0af8d97f7ba",
                                                "sense_id": "03b3028c-8d04-3fd2-95b2-5214bc17481c",
                                                "text": "A contributing factor to this slightly regressive femininity may have been the sugary fabrics (silver lamé, tulle over sequins) and the meringuelike puffs and baby Googums bows at the neck."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e42cd28-b2b9-4337-b7bc-1e2093dafcb9",
                                                "sense_id": "03b3028c-8d04-3fd2-95b2-5214bc17481c",
                                                "text": "One outcome of the idea of fluid masculinity and femininity is the notion of genderqueerness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b7b65a58-2785-445c-9719-b33e128c04f2",
                        "source_entry_id": "cb4ca7b4-680d-3ddd-a6d3-7e2854c74db0",
                        "source_sense_id": "f104ab45-8c5c-3b5b-908c-f307fe3aa333",
                        "target_lang_word": "feminineness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "feminineness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8e1cbba-0b89-3c64-8433-a64631f41f6d",
                                        "entry_id": "8b95c69b-cc03-3025-ae94-048e44f73361",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state or condition of being feminine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ca8654ee-a23f-42d1-892b-7bcd77e42006",
                        "source_entry_id": "cb4ca7b4-680d-3ddd-a6d3-7e2854c74db0",
                        "source_sense_id": "f104ab45-8c5c-3b5b-908c-f307fe3aa333",
                        "target_lang_word": "féminité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "féminité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd25dbbf-567b-33b8-ad24-7dbfe5850223",
                                        "entry_id": "277f2ff9-5812-3e58-b2fc-5d7af94594ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Caractère de ce qui est féminin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8fcfcc7-13ab-4e20-b508-829710376b5a",
                                                "sense_id": "bd25dbbf-567b-33b8-ad24-7dbfe5850223",
                                                "text": "Le vaisseau de la féminité : galbée en proue, majestueuse en poupe et poivrée dans les écoutilles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef2d2ce0-de2f-4f74-80ca-22d84a26ee05",
                                                "sense_id": "bd25dbbf-567b-33b8-ad24-7dbfe5850223",
                                                "text": "Mais priver la femme de sa féminité ne peut-être qu’un appauvrissement pour elle et pour l’humanité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5bba0db-47a7-4590-95b1-e441f298f681",
                                                "sense_id": "bd25dbbf-567b-33b8-ad24-7dbfe5850223",
                                                "text": "Ainsi, la complicité particulière de Juliette avec sa mère est patente. Parfois, vous les garçons, vous vous en amusiez de façon un peu pincée : la sœusœur n’étant pas exactement « traitée » comme vous. Ce n’est pas que votre mère la préfère, c’est qu’il y a entre elles une promesse de femme, les prémices d’un lien de chair et de féminité qui leur font se dire des confidences qui nous échappent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91ebf0ce-0005-4651-9da9-9acbd94280d8",
                                                "sense_id": "bd25dbbf-567b-33b8-ad24-7dbfe5850223",
                                                "text": "Dans les interactions sociales, la seule différence entre mon genre transsexuel et leurs genres cissexuels c'est que ma féminité est souvent caractérisée comme secondaire, illégitime, ou comme une imitation de leur féminité."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
